Sidewalks are required on all street frontages regardless of the zoning district in which the street is located. Notwithstanding anything contained in this chapter to the contrary, sidewalks shall be created as follows:
(1) Sidewalks and curb ramps shall be constructed in all new development or redevelopment along all abutting or internal streets, existing or new, private or public, for the entire property frontage.
(2) The following permits and activities shall require the installation of sidewalk along all roadway frontages of the affected property:
a. Development permits;
b. Land disturbance permits;
c. Building permits;
d. All commercial, industrial, office or multi-family construction located on any street;
e. Subdivision of property that creates a new public or private street (minimum one (1) side of the street); and
f. Nonresidential subdivision plat or nonresidential combination plat.
( Ord. No. 2019-01 , § 1, 7-3-2019)

